    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` and made the API return it.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a `@Transient getIdentityKey()` that derives `telephone + \"|\" + email + \"|\" + householdId`, with each absent component rendered as `\"\"`. This lives on the entity alongside the other derived getters (`displayName`, `membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`, \u2026), so identity-key derivation has a single home.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps `owner.getIdentityKey()` into responses (verified in the generated mapper).\n\n3. **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 replaced the now-obsolete `findOwnerByTelephone` and `findOwnersByEmail` facade queries with a single `findOwnersByIdentityKey(String)` that filters existing owners by whole-key equality. `findOwnersInSameHousehold` stays (still used by `joinHousehold`).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 removed the three separate telephone/email/household duplicate checks and replaced them with one identity-key check. The check runs *after* `joinHousehold` assigns the shared `householdId`, so the key is complete. The old \"same last name + address\" household rejection is gone \u2014 two household members with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a 409.\n\n5. **Exceptions** \u2014 introduced `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409, reporting the `identityKey` field) and its handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`; deleted the three superseded exception classes and their handlers.\n\nThe behaviour change is exactly as specified: rejection now occurs only when a new owner's whole `identityKey` equals an existing owner's, and `identityKey` is returned on the owner resource.",
